  <h2>Normalize before you paste into Kakobuy</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strip tracking wrappers:</strong> unwrap nested redirects until you recover marketplace-stable HTTPS URLs—protocol recap in <a href="/blog/kakobuy-links-discovery-url-hygiene/">links hygiene essay</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Prefer desktop-class permalinks:</strong> mobile-only shortlinks frequently omit variant parameters essential for <a href="/blog/kakobuy-weidian/">Weidian</a> fidelity.</li>
    <li><strong>Capture forwarded timestamps:</strong> Telegram edits messages silently; snapshot context cells noting channel + message date.</li>
    <li><strong>Assume media vanishes:</strong> hosted videos/images may expire—mirror critical stills ethically or cite archival strategy from <a href="/blog/spreadsheet-row-archiving-vanished-listings/">listing mortality essay</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why this complements—not replaces—Discord literacy</h2>
  <p>
    Our <a href="/blog/kakobuy-discord/">Discord primer</a> still applies to raffle psychology and coupon rumours.
    Telegram simply introduces distinct forwarding graphs; moderators should train helpers to log <strong>source channel identity</strong> because impersonation clones circulate faster during mega-sales chronicled in <a href="/blog/taobao-tmall-618-2026-spreadsheet-forwarding-rhythm/">618 rhythm essay</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Primary-service references</h2>
  <p>
    Telegram publishes general FAQ/security guidance at <a href="https://telegram.org/faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">telegram.org/faq</a>; specific bot behaviours vary—never assume third-party scrapers respect ToS.
